  "dom_id": "step-q110314",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Mel is buying a skateboard. The price of a skateboard is $P$ dollars, and Mel also has to pay a $18%$ tax.\n\nWhat expression represents the total cost, in dollars, of a skateboard after tax is applied?",
  "worked_solution": "The price before taxes of a skateboard is $P$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of tax Mel pays is  $18%$ of the price of a skateboard, or $0.18P.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the skateboard after tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nP+0.18P\n$$",
